# Trivy vulnerability ignore list — STRUCTURED, REVIEWED, TIME-BOXED (WS5 / #1100)
#
# Every entry MUST follow this exact 4-field format or it is INVALID and does
# NOT suppress anything (CI fails on invalid entries):
#
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN # <reason> # <reviewer> # <expiry-date-YYYY-MM-DD>
#
# Rule | Explanation
# ------|------------------------------------------------------------
# reason  | Non-empty justification: which dependency/toolchain, why unfixable,
#          and what tracking issue exists (e.g. "upstream issue #482; rebuild after
#          next base image release").
# reviewer| GitHub handle of the human who approved the exception.
# expiry  | ISO date (YYYY-MM-DD). After this date the entry is EXPIRED and CI
#          FAILS until it is re-reviewed and re-expired or the CVE is fixed.
#
# These exceptions are for UPSTREAM / BASE-IMAGE CVEs with no available fix
# only. New dependencies introduced by a PR are never suppressible here — a PR
# that adds a package carrying a CRITICAL or HIGH CVE fails CI regardless.

# Example of a valid entry (uncomment + fill in real values to use):
# CVE-2024-47176 # OpenSSH in base image, patched upstream after next release; tracking #000 # reviewer: octocat # 2026-12-31